plan and is one of the most  powerful ways to capture the attention  of your target audience and motivate  them to convert or purchase copywriting  is everywhere when you go online or even  offline remember the google ad that you  see when you search for something in  google that is a copy or if you check  your email box you will find different  promotional mails by different companies  that are a copy  basically those companies are trying to  convince you to take some action it can  be anything for example an e-commerce  company will convince you to purchase  some of their stored products  now let's talk about the copywriting  formula a good copy usually follows aida  formula a stands for attention i for  interest d for desire and a for action  almost every good copywriter uses this  formula to write better copies and it's  important for you in case you decided to  become a copywriter or want to use  copywriting in some of your work so i  hope now we understand what actually  copywriting is now let's try to  understand what does a copywriter  actually do  the copywriter's job is to write words  that convince an audience to take some  action for the benefit of the company in  which the writer works  let's have a look at sample copyrighted  job description that will help you  understand the role and responsibilities  and the skills needed for this role  so firstly let's have a look at  responsibilities writing editing and  publishing engaging content for various  social media network including facebook  twitter instagram linkedin and google my  business optimizing social media post  language tone message based on your  target audience behavior selecting  appealing images and videos to  complement text for designers to design  the post  let's have a look at some more  responsibilities coordinate with  internal teams to create advertising  posts for client respond to questions  and comments on social media pages  promptly and accurately  there can be more responsibilities to a  copywriter depending on what the company  needs so it varies from company to  company now let's see what skills a  company looks for in a copywriter  hands-on experience using various social  media platform to advertise solid  knowledge of seo keyword research and  analytics tools example google analytics  familiarity with online paid advertising  let's have a look of some others  requirement and skills  ability to deliver creative web content  text image and video excellent  communication skills  so now we know what copywriter does  let's explore its various types  seo copywriting it means optimizing the  copy using keywords to make it rank at  the top of the search results for  example if you optimize a company's  product page correctly through seo  copywriting then there is a high chances  that your sales page would rank at the  top of the search result which would  result in more sales next we have social  media copywriting this type of  copywriting is used on social media  platform for example a catchy title is  used to grab the attention of the user  and emoji is used to make the copy  interesting or frame the right message  in order to convince the audience to  take some kind of action  next we have technical copywriting the  motive for writing technical copy is to  explain the latest technologies or the  technical product that the company wants  to sell for example if you have a tech  product you need a copywriter who can  explain the technical aspect use case of  the product and how that product helped  the customer direct response copywriting  it is a type of communication that is  compelling enough to be able to  influence the customers to act  in other words any copy that encourages  the recipient to act immediately and the  response from the reader are miserable  another type of copywriting is public  relation copywriting in public relation  copywriting you write newsworthy things  to catch your audience attention and  gain their trust it helps you quickly  earn an audience with credible sources  and as a result your business can  promote its product and services more  effectively whenever you search on  google you see some ads at the top of  the search results that are also made up  using copywriting following that next we  have ad copywriting this type of  copywriting is used to create effective  ads generally it's used in facebook and  google ads now we reached the second  last type of copywriting in the list  which is email copywriting as you  understood by the name all the copy that  we use in emails are email copywriting  it includes a good subject line nice  preview text an intro sentence for the  body of your email and a strong call to  action  now let's discuss our last type which is  brand copywriting brand recognition and  connecting with customer begin with  communicating what your brand represents  your brand image can be conveyed through  writing it can be in the form of logo a  song or a phrase to create brand copy  you have to think about your customers  first with this we have come to the end  of this copywriting types list before  jumping into the next topic i have a  task for you just pause this video and  in the comment box type your favorite  type of copywriting i hope you are done  with the comment  let's move forward to our next topic  which is difference between copywriting  and content writing  firstly let's discuss the difference  based on the overall goal  copywriting is a type of writing aimed  at selling a brand on the other hand  content writing is all about building a  perception in consumer's mind the next  difference is based on the length of the  content a copywriter typically writes  short form of copy and a content writer  writes long form of copy text written by  copywriter is brief and engaging content  writer often have to write more in-depth  content explaining a process or topic  now what's the difference when it comes  to a role in a company a copywriter is  someone whose primary role is to create  copy and a content writer often does  more than just write it may be a writer  blogger executive or anyone else  lastly let's discuss the difference  based on seo a good copywriter  understand seo but when it comes to a  good content writer they should know  about the advanced seo  now let's explore some of the helpful  tools for a copywriter copy ai it's an  ai tool and the greatest thing about  this tool is it's very simple to use you  can generate instagram caption product  description and even product value  proposition by just providing a few  words it's a paid tool but it has a 7  days free trial the next tool that we  have is grammarly grammarly is a free  online tool that finds mistakes in your  writing and suggests improvements as you  write grammarly will underline any  mistake you have made and offer  suggestions on how to fix them  additionally it has a plagiarism checker  and a punctuation checker however for  additional features you need to go with  grammarly premium  what tune with the help of grammarly you  can fix your writing mistakes but when  it comes to rephrase and rewording your  content without sacrificing flow tone or  meaning word tune came into the picture  hence the combination of grammarly and  word tune is the best for the copywriter  and it's a paid tool but have a free  plan for beginners  the last tool in our bucket is wordsmith  if you rely on data in your day-to-day  decisions wordsmith is a perfect for you  it can be used for everything from  journalism to financial reporting  because it produces natural sounding  content simply create one template and  set up a few variables and wordsmith  will generate multiple alternative  scripts for example you can write  chatbot scripts for responding to  various complex customer requests  now comes the most interesting and the  last topic of a session the average  salary of a copywriter several factors  determine the income a person can expect  including experience the size of your  company your location and your industry  copywriters are the brain behind  advertisements explaining what the  product does and why people should buy  it they are also responsible for shaping  the brand's identity and tone of voice  copywriters are a valuable resources for  businesses as they are responsible for  writing the first impression customers  get of a company a copywriter earns  approximately 3 lakh 64 000 per annum in  india and in the us he she can earn  roughly 53 000  and when it comes to a senior copywriter  the average salary in india is 5 flag 86  000 per annum and in the u.s he she can  roughly earn 78 000  per year  so with this we have come to the end of  the session on copywriting i hope the  session was informative and exciting in  case you have questions about any of the  topics covered in the session or if you  need resources used in this session then  please feel free to let us know in the  comment section below and our team of  practitioners will be more than happy to  resolve all your queries at the earliest  until next time this is tushar from the  simply learn team signing off thank you  stay safe and keep  learning hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learn youtube  channel and click here to watch similar  videos turn it up and get certified  click here

